    "title": "Award-winning Hawaii architect, design leader dies - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Talia Agliam ,\n3 hours ago HONOLULU (HawaiiNewsNow) - An award-winning Hawaii architect, whose designs helped shape Hawaii’s modern landscape, has died. Francis S. Oda died Saturday, Feb. 14, surrounded by family. Oda helped found the design firm G70 in 1971, and received over 50 awards for his architectural work, which includes the Four Seasons... Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 3",
